<Item XName="Text" Type="Param">
<DataEntry>&apos;The bitstream of L1CD signal is modulated on L1 carrier frequency using BOC (1, 1) modulation, with a subcarrier&#x000D;&#x000A;frequency of 1.023 MHz and a chipping rate of 1.023 Mbps. Each bit of the bitstream is applied to a BOC(1,1)&#x000D;&#x000A;spreading symbol consisting of one cycle of a 1.023 MHz squarewave, defined as binary 10 (1= positive binary bit&#x000D;&#x000A;value, see Figure 3.3-2a) with total duration 1/1.023 microseconds. The BOC(1,1) spreading symbols are defined&#x000D;&#x000A;using sine-phasing, so are aligned with bits of L1CD-code. Contrary to convention, a &#x201C;0&#x201D; is in-phase with the carrier&#x000D;&#x000A;and a &#x201C;1&#x201D; is 180 out of phase with the carrier.</DataEntry></Item></Item>
